# 🚀 Page Based on Float & Borders – CSS Basics

## 📌 Overview

This project represents my **second CSS project**, where I started experimenting with **Float layouts** and **Borders**.

It is a static webpage designed to practice:

- Floating elements to structure content  
- Adding borders for visual separation and styling  
- Basic layout design with CSS  

🔗 **Live Demo:**  
https://abdelrahmangalal200101-cpu.github.io/Page-Based-On-Float-Borders-Css/

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- HTML5  
- CSS3  
- CSS Float  
- Borders & Box Model  

---

## 🎯 What I Learned

- How to float elements to create multi-column layouts  
- Styling elements with borders for better visual hierarchy  
- Understanding the Box Model in CSS  
- Combining CSS properties for clean layouts  
- Preparing for more advanced layout techniques like Flex and Grid  

---

## 📈 Progress Note

This project shows the **early stages of my CSS journey**, right after learning HTML basics.

It laid the foundation for **more advanced layouts using Flexbox, Grid, and positioning**, and helped me understand how to structure content visually and effectively.
